  "final_answer_preview": "According to Section 14 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023, nothing is considered an offence if it is done by a person who, due to a mistake of fact (and not a mistake of law), believes in good faith that they are bound by law to perform that act. This is further supported by Section 17, which states that a person who believes themselves to be justified by law due to a mistake of fact is also not committing an offence. Therefore, if someone acts under a genuine misunderstanding of the facts, they may be protected from legal liability.",
